1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,905
[A] You can do spot DEXes,

2
00:00:00,905 --> 00:00:03,454
but they're constrained to the number of assets they can list.

3
00:00:03,454 --> 00:00:05,468
If you're in DeFi and you're trading on Uniswap,

4
00:00:05,468 --> 00:00:07,811
you can only trade assets that are tokenized on Ethereum.

5
00:00:07,811 --> 00:00:09,496
So you can trade wBTC, you can trade ETH,

6
00:00:09,496 --> 00:00:11,346
obviously wrapped SOL, there's some of that.

7
00:00:11,346 --> 00:00:12,867
The further down you get on the list,

8
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:14,306
once it's no longer Ethereum-based,

9
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:15,251
you're kind of screwed.

10
00:00:15,251 --> 00:00:17,018
It's so annoying to have to wrap and unwrap

11
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:18,375
and figure out exactly, you know,

12
00:00:18,375 --> 00:00:19,814
what you own and how to get it out.

13
00:00:19,814 --> 00:00:22,363
What really people want is the centralized exchange experience,

14
00:00:22,363 --> 00:00:24,459
which is just, I'm actually trading the underlying.

15
00:00:24,459 --> 00:00:25,898
That's, I think, part of the reason

16
00:00:25,898 --> 00:00:27,950
why Near Intents has taken off, is it's so simple.

